<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Required. Under the hardened runtime the microphone is gated by this
      entitlement *before* TCC is ever consulted: without it the process is
      refused at the runtime level, so no prompt appears and the app never shows
      up in System Settings > Privacy & Security > Microphone at all.

      That failure is silent and looks nothing like a permissions problem —
      AVAudioEngine starts, sockets bind, status reports listening, and not one
      word is ever transcribed. NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in Info.plist is
      necessary but not sufficient; both have to be present.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
      Camera, same gate as above: entitlement here *and*
      NSCameraUsageDescription in Info.plist, or the app never appears under
      Privacy & Security > Camera. See spec §4, "Permissions — verify each,
      assume none". That table also lists system audio as "verify" for both
      the Info.plist key and the entitlement — Engine owns confirming what
      Core Audio taps need under the hardened runtime and adding it here.
      Screen and window capture need no entitlement; ScreenCaptureKit raises
      the TCC prompt itself.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
